<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:64:default:gcc">
<!--
    A call drops the arguments its caller compares with each other first.

        double elapsed(long a, long b);           /* no body, no prototype */
        int newer(const struct stamp *s, const struct stamp *ref)
        {
            if (s->sec == ref->sec &amp;&amp; s->nsec == ref->nsec)
                return 0;
            return elapsed(s->sec, ref->sec) + (s->nsec - ref->nsec) / 1e9 > 0.0;
        }
        long differ(const struct stamp *s, const struct stamp *ref)
        { if (s->sec == ref->sec) return 0; return other(s->sec, ref->sec) + 1; }

    clang 22 -O2 (-fno-builtin -fno-stack-protector -fcf-protection=none,
    linked -nostdlib -static -Ttext=0x401000; elapsed and other are
    PLT-shaped stubs, `jmp *slot(%rip)`, as an import is).  Each caller loads both values
    into rdi and rsi, compares them there (`cmp %rsi,%rdi; jne`) and calls.
    onlyOpUse rejected both trials because the compare feeds a branch, and
    kuna printed `elapsed()` and `other() + 1`.  find's `pred_newer` calls
    `difftime` the same way.

    Stage: P4 active input-trial scoring (kuna_comparedarg.rs, always on).
    At a direct call to a callee with no body to read, a compare of the value
    with another argument of the same call is no competing use; a compare
    with anything else still is.
-->
